'''anadrom''' (an′a̤-drom), ''n.'' [< Gr. ἀνάδρομος, running up, applied to fish ascending rivers, < ἀναδραμεῖν, run up, < ἀνά, up, + δραμεῖν, run: see ''dromedary''.] An anadromous fish; one which ascends rivers from the sea to spawn.

'''anadromous''' (a-nad′rọ̄-mus), ''a.'' [< Gr. ἀνάδρομος: see ''anadrom''.] Ascending. {{smaller|Applied—(''a'') In ''zoöl.'', to fishes which pass from the sea to fresh water to spawn.}}

